WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.634
-Our first guest tonight is

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.468
a best-selling author

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.602
and comedian whose new comedy

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:04.704
special, "Revolution,"

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.673
will premiere
on Netflix December 27th.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.341
Please welcome back to the show
one of our favorites,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.975
Chelsea Handler, everybody!

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:11.844
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:14.847
[ Funk plays ]

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:23.389 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.458 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.460
Welcome back!

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.794
It's so lovely to have you here.

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.597
-Oh, my God, I'm always happy
to be with you, Seth.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.898
-And it's kind of --
it was maybe a little angsty

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:34.901
the beginning of last week
and here we are, you know,

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.836
six days after the midterms.
How are you feeling?

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.938
-Oh, God. Well, you know,
I'm a staunch Republican.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.473
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.941
And you keep your spirit up.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.044
-I know. I'm so woke that
I've become a Republican.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.145
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.279
I was pretty excited.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:48.614
You know,
it's a pretty exciting time.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:51.217
It's been a long time
since I've watched an election

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.753
where I was like surprised
and hopeful.

00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:57.390
And then there are
just so many doorknobs

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.460
that are also involved in this
election, like Herschel Walker

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.061
-Yeah.
-and Lauren Boebert.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:05.298
And I'm just like Republicans
have completely lost the plot.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:08.634
So, to see them
actively losing their ground

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:12.605
and thinking about just Trump
pacing back and forth

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.841
at Mar-A-Lago just gave me

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.876
so much joy.
-I did have empathy for --

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.378
[ Laughter ]
for Tiffany Trump

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.280
on her wedding day,
that that was when --

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.482
I think Nevada was called

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.116
while he was probably
at the wedding.

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:26.119
-Yeah, but she was -- I mean,
for her to get married

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.354
at her father's place
was a mistake, to begin with...

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.189
-Yeah.
-...because, I mean,
it's not like --

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.257
I'm sure he charged her,
you know?
-Yeah.

00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:34.026
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.
-So why?

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:35.561
I mean, she's not
thinking things through.

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:36.696
She's marrying some guy

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.231
who comes
from a very rich family.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.967
She needs to cut ties now
and just be done with him.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.202
If anything,
she should've scheduled

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:44.737
a wedding at Mar-A-Lago,

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.706
but had the real
wedding elsewhere, right?

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.808
[ Laughter ]
Get him going to the place.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.077
Because he would've stayed there
and it would've taken hours

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.412
before he realized
the wedding wasn't happening.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.447
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.149
-But also, can you imagine
trying to celebrate with him

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.518
about anything,
even if he was in a good mood?

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:02.055
I mean, this is an opportunity
for her to find

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.956
her real birth father, you know?

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.258
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.393
Now that she's married,
she can sever ties

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.529
and go live a full life
where she's treated like,

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.831
you know, not a marginalized
member of a family.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.166
-That's a very -- This is --
See? This is good advice.

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.636
And I want to draw attention
to the fact that it makes

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.337
natural sense to me that you're
good at advice.

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.206
You started a podcast

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.741
where you're now
giving advice to people.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.010
-I do.
I like to give advice,

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.179
whether it's solicited
or unsolicited.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.513
[ Laughter ]
-I think that's what everyone
appreciates about you --

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:28.681
-You know?
-you don't have to ask.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.982
You just give it.
-No, yeah.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:31.350
I mean, and I love to like

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.085
give girls a little bit
more power

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.720
when you're feeling insecure.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.423
As women, we go through so many
different phases of our lives

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.457
where we feel self-confident

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:40.059
and then
we second-guess ourselves.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.729
And I'm just like I want women
to be empowered, you know?

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.331
Also, when you see something,
to say something, you know?

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.734
And I use a story
that I like to tell

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:51.637
as a guideline for all people,
you know, to say something,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.939
even if it's
a very awkward situation.
-Okay.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.676
-I once accidentally had dinner
with Woody Allen and Soon-Yi.

00:02:57.676 --> 00:02:59.312
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:02.148
How does that come about
by accident?

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.983
-Well, I blame Katie Couric
because she's the one

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.585
who invited me out that night
and then, before I knew it,

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:09.222
I was sitting across
from Soon-Yi and Woody Allen.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.423
And, as a woman,
knowing what I know,

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:12.992
that was hard for me.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.461
I wasn't -- I was like,
"I don't trust myself,"

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.963
because I can't really be
respectful, you know?

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:21.333
[ Laughter ]
And I didn't know what was going
to come out of my mouth,

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:22.936
if I was going to be able
to control myself,

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.838
but I was like, "Just wait,
you know, like wait your time

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.207
and just bide your time
and just, you know,

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:31.810
be pleasant and be respectful
during this dinner encounter."

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.147
And I waited and I was patient
and I exercised patience.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:38.617
And then dessert came and they
put down a blackberry cobbler

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:40.286
in front of Soon-Yi and Woody

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.555
and Woody went to take a bite
out of the blackberry cobbler

00:03:43.555 --> 00:03:44.757
and I leaned in and said,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.225
"How did you two meet?"

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:49.162
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:54.233
-That's real patience.
That's an assassin's patience.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.768
[ Laughter ]
-I mean, I slept like
a baby that night.

00:03:56.768 --> 00:03:57.736
You know what I mean?

00:03:57.736 --> 00:03:59.038
I was just like,
"You know what?"

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.474
And then Katie's like,
"Okay, Chelsea, time to go."

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.542
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.610
And, yeah, but I feel like
women need

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.146
to always be able to because,
if I had left that dinner

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.547
and I hadn't said anything,

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:11.050
I would've been so pissed
at myself for years to come.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.185
So, I think, you know,
I'm a good big sister

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:15.221
and I want everyone to succeed
and I just want everybody

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.423
to be a little smarter
and a little braver.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.526
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Well, those are --
that's wonderful advice.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:23.696
You you went out --
We were talking backstage.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.531
You toured this hour.
You have a new hour

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.032
that's coming out soon,
called "Revolution."

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:29.635
-"Revolution," Netflix,
two days after Christmas.

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:32.705
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Almost -- was it 100 cities
or thereabouts?

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.573
-Yeah, I did about 100.

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:35.941
I did about 120 days.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:38.711
I'm still -- I'm finishing up
my last bit of this tour.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.347
I'm actually headed to Florida,
so I can't wait to see

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.416
how that works out.
This weekend, everybody.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.651
All the Democrats in Florida,
I'm coming!

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:47.487
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, there's a lot of them.
-Come see me.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.721
Yeah.
There's about four left.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.324
[ Laughter ]
So, yeah, I've been touring

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.891
and, I mean,
first of all, I love touring.

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:54.726
You love stand-up.
We both doing it.
-I do, yeah.

00:04:54.726 --> 00:04:57.230
-Yeah.
-And you shot it
in Nashville, right?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.997
-Uh-huh, yeah.
-That's a great comedy town.

00:04:58.997 --> 00:05:00.833
-It's a great theater,
the Ryman in Nashville.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:04.537
So, I loved -- You know, I had
so much material from COVID

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:07.673
and from just all the stuff
that happens during COVID,

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:11.710
you know, and all of like
just how we all behaved,

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.913
how embarrassing it was,
starting with yourself,

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.414
-Yes.
-you know?
I was Windex ing my food

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:17.550
up until recently, so.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.385
You know, and now,
you're just like, "What, COVID?

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.187
What's that?"
I was excited for monkeypox

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:22.788
to take off,
but that didn't seem --

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.123
[ Laughter ]
-I'm sorry.
I know you were real--

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.525
You were one
of the early investors.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.160
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I know.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.761
It's just like Bitcoin.

00:05:29.761 --> 00:05:31.397
It's just one big bubble.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.398
-Yeah. Monkeycoin

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.200
did not work out for me.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.170
You actually talk a little bit
about being a businesswoman

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.204
at a very young age
in your special

00:05:39.204 --> 00:05:41.940
and the fact that you started
a babysitting service.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.542
-Oh, yeah. Well, when I was
ten years old --

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:44.977
I'm the youngest
of six kids, you guys,

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.779
so, when I was born,
my family was just like,

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.847
"You know, let her raise
herself, I guess."

00:05:48.847 --> 00:05:51.083
[ Laughter ]
They were sleeping most
of the time

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:54.220
and they just had been exhausted
by my other siblings.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.155
So, when I was ten, I took my
first plane ride to California

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:58.491
to visit our grandparents

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.760
and it was my mom
and like two of my brothers

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.395
and I had never been on a plane.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.030
So, we walked past
the first-class section

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.999
and I was like, "Oh, like
who are these people," you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:08.901
And my mom's like,
"Never mind that, you know.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.269
We have six kids in our family.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:13.138
We can't afford that and we'll
never fly first-class."

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:15.040
And I'm just like,
"Speak for yourself," you know?

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.109
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:18.644
And we went to go visit
my grandparents.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.946
We came home and I was like,
"I have to start a business,"

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:22.949
so I started
a babysitting company.

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:25.818
I was ten years old,
but I looked like I was 15,

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.587
so, I lied and said I was 15
and ended up babysitting

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.089
for kids
that were older than me.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.424
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:34.326
As a ten-year-old, I had
a regular client who was 14

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:37.129
and I was basically putting
this kid in time-outs

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:40.433
all summer long,
but I saved up like $3,500

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:42.668
and then the next time
we went on a plane ride,

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.237
it was three years later,
I was 13 years old,

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:48.440
and I had gotten a first-class
ticket from a travel agent

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.042
that lived down the street
and so,

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.778
when we boarded the plane
with my mother

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:55.113
and my two sisters, this time,
I saw my seat 2A and I said,

00:06:55.113 --> 00:06:56.581
"See you guys
at the end of the flight."

00:06:56.581 --> 00:06:59.585
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.988
-I have a great deal more
to ask you.

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:04.356
We'll be right back

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:07.026
[ Cheering and applause ]
with more from Chelsea Handler.

